From: Wineforge contributors <wineforge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:20:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] winebus.sys: Disable IOHID by default on macOS

Starting the IOHID backend can cause macOS to request Input Monitoring access
during fresh-prefix initialization, even when the device callback later rejects
every non-controller device.  Desktop applications do not need this access.

Keep the backend available behind the existing Wine bus-options registry key.
Users who need direct IOHID controller support can set "Enable IOHID" to "Y".
---
 dlls/winebus.sys/main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
@@ -802,7 +802,7 @@ static NTSTATUS fdo_pnp_dispatch(DEVICE_OBJECT *device, IRP *irp)
         if (!check_bus_option(L"Enable SDL", 1) || sdl_driver_init())
         {
             udev_driver_init();
-            iohid_driver_init();
+            if (check_bus_option(L"Enable IOHID", 0)) iohid_driver_init();
         }
         xbox_driver_init();

-- 
2.50.1
